 } } \right]$$<br><br>$$\left| A \right| = 4{x^3} - 4{x^2} - 4x = f(x)$$<br><br>$$f'(x) = 4(3{x^2} - 2x - 1) = 0$$<br><br>$$ \Rightarrow x = 1;x = {{ - 1} \over 3}$$<br><br>$$\therefore$$ $$f(1) =  - 4;f\left( { - {1 \over 3}} \right) = {{20} \over {27}}$$<br><br>Sum $$ =  - 4 + {{20} \over 7} =  - {{88} \over {27}}$$

