 } $$<br><br>Here [ a ] = n<br><br>Now, $$\int_0^a {{e^{x - [x]}}} dx = 10e - 9$$<br><br>$$ \Rightarrow \int\limits_0^n {{e^{\{ x\} }}dx}  + \int\limits_n^a {{e^{x - [x]}}dx}  = 10e - 9$$<br><br>$$\therefore$$ $$n\int\limits_0^1 {{e^x}dx}  + \int\limits_n^a {{e^{x - n}}dx}  = 10e - 9$$<br><br>$$ \Rightarrow n(e - 1) + ({e^{a - n}} - 1) = 10e - 9$$<br><br>$$\therefore$$ n = 0 and {a} = log<sub>e</sub> 2<br><br>So, $$a = [a] + \{ a\}  = (10 + {\log _e}2)$$<br><br>$$\Rightarrow$$ Option (2) is correct.

