   {f(9x)} &amp; {0 \le x \le 1}  \cr 
   0 &amp; {1 \le x \le 3}  \cr 
   { - 1} &amp; {3 &lt; x \le 4}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$<br><br>g(x) is continuous<br><br>$$g'(x) = \left[ {\matrix{
   {3(x - 1)(x - 3)} &amp; {0 \le x \le 1}  \cr 
   0 &amp; {1 \le x \le 3}  \cr 
   { - 1} &amp; {3 &lt; x \le 4}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$<br><br>g(x) is non-differentiable at x = 3

