<br><br>$$\left| {\matrix{
   {y + 1} &amp; \alpha  &amp; \beta   \cr 
   \alpha  &amp; {y + \beta } &amp; 1  \cr 
   \beta  &amp; 1 &amp; {y + \alpha }  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>= $$\left| {\matrix{
   {y + 1} &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   \omega  &amp; {y + {\omega ^2}} &amp; 1  \cr 
   {{\omega ^2}} &amp; 1 &amp; {y + \omega }  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>C<sub>1</sub> $$ \to $$ C<sub>1</sub> + C<sub>2</sub> + C<sub>3</sub>
<br><br>= $$\left| {\matrix{
   {y + 1 + \omega  + {\omega ^2}} &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   {y + 1 + \omega  + {\omega ^2}} &amp; {y + {\omega ^2}} &amp; 1  \cr 
   {y + 1 + \omega  + {\omega ^2}} &amp; 1 &amp; {y + \omega }  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>= $$\left| {\matrix{
   y &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   y &amp; {y + {\omega ^2}} &amp; 1  \cr 
   y &amp; 1 &amp; {y + \omega }  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>As $$1 + \omega  + {\omega ^2}$$ = 0
<br><br>= $$y\left| {\matrix{
   1 &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   1 &amp; {y + {\omega ^2}} &amp; 1  \cr 
   1 &amp; 1 &amp; {y + \omega }  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>R<sub>2</sub> $$ \to $$ R<sub>2</sub> - R<sub>1</sub>
<br>R<sub>3</sub> $$ \to $$ R<sub>3</sub> - R<sub>1</sub>
<br><br>= $$y\left| {\matrix{
   1 &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   0 &amp; {y + {\omega ^2} - \omega } &amp; {1 - {\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   0 &amp; {1 - \omega } &amp; {y + \omega  - {\omega ^2}}  \cr 

 } } \right|$$
<br><br>= y$$\left[ {\left( {y + {\omega ^2} - \omega } \right)\left( {y + \omega  - {\omega ^2}} \right) - \left( {1 - {\omega ^2}} \right)\left( {1 - \omega } \right)} \right]$$
<br><br>= y(y<sup>2</sup>) = y<sup>3</sup>

